# twinBASIC build output
Build/

# twinBASIC export: vendored/regeneratable package + type library copies.
# `export` bundles full copies of every referenced compiler package (VB/VBA/VBRUN
# compatibility layers, WinNativeCommonCtls, etc.) into the exported tree - this is not
# project-specific source, it's twinBASIC's own framework code, resolved again from the local
# package cache on import. Only Sources/, Settings, Resources/ and References/ are the
# project's own content.
# Confirmed (2026-09-23): importing from a src/ tree with these folders empty still resolves
# the referenced packages cleanly from twinBASIC's own central package store on import.
src/Packages/
src/ImportedTypeLibraries/

# Machine-specific export script (contains local paths to the twinBASIC install and the
# .twinproj file). Copy export.bat.example to export.bat and fill in the paths for your own
# machine. Bringing changes back into the .twinproj works through the IDE instead (see
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), so there is no import.bat.
export.bat

# OS cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
